WEBVTT

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:05.530
We got lots of goodies for ya today, kids.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:06.250
Huh?

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.990
Hey, they're all the plain white ones!

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.640
Over here, mommy!

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.500
Those kids just never run out of steam, do they?

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.020
Locally grown cucumbers!

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.620
And you know what, mommy? They said I was the best!

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.550
Good for you.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.800
M-Marry me!

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.050
Okay!

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.710
Is this your first time in the capital, Rygart?

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.660
Nah, I came here once when I was just a squirt.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.060
My dad brought me.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.580
Wow, that's awesome!

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.650
Rygart!

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.400
Can you move?

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:00.120
Are you okay, Rygart?

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.720
Yeah...

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:03.940
Hey, pops?

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:11.090
What'd you say? I can't hear you.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.080
Were heading back to Binonten.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.690
The three of you, watch our backs
and keep an eye out! Don't get caught!

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:19.700
Yes, sir!

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:29.320
Refugees coming from the north, sir.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.390
Let them in!

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.900
Standby until the escort troops return!

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.680
Make sure the palace is sufficiently guarded!

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.890
A riot's broken out at the central shelter!

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.650
I thought they'd appointed a spokesman!

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.590
How goes the boarding at the harbor?

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.420
Where has King Hodr gone to?

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.410
The troops are gathering in the
town square! Where are the generals?

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.840
I can't find His Majesty anywhere!

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.040
Relocate to the eastern garrison!

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:59.290
Damn it! What's the Guard doing?!

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:52.510
This is regrettable.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:55.950
And by that I do not mean the loss of Bades.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:04:02.520
To meet a highly skillful pilot that's capable of bringing
out the full potential of these faulty model Artemis.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:06.190
And knowing that I'll never be
able to cross blades with him again.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.860
Too bad.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:14.740
We'll move ahead to take Binonten,
there'll be no adjustments in the plan.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.620
Now...

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:20.680
It's time for you to answer my questions.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:26.620
Why was such an incompetent man
chosen to be the pilot of the black Golem?

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:31.390
I fail to understand Krishna.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:35.010
That was most likely a Golem from ancient technology.

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:38.310
A machine capable of changing the tide of this war.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.450
Why?

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:44.380
Because he's an idiot.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.330
Colonel.

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:09.750
Yes sir.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:15.250
It seems that one of Valkyrie squadron's soldiers,
Cleo, has been held prisoner there for some time.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:18.040
The Zaubraff's daughter, to be exact.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.380
The report hasn't been verified yet, however.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.090
I'll go find out.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:23.700
If the intel's correct, I'll rescue her.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:29.050
Rescuing the princess would be the icing on the cake.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:31.920
I've neither the right nor reason to stop you.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:32.650
Understood.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.620
Now... Let us begin.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:39.550
All that's left are the enemy survivors.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.560
Let's go. Prepare to move out.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:44.350
Yes sir!

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:58.700
Move out!

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.230
So that's what happened...

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:23.340
Yeah.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.080
What about Narvi and the guys?

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.300
Did you find them?

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.650
Yes.

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:39.300
We noticed them after we found you.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:41.320
The enemy battalion is on the move.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:43.190
They number 90 units.

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:46.310
Borcuse is planning to advance under the cover of darkness.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.920
We can't afford to rest here.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:50.990
Can you handle it?

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:52.370
No problem!
Yes, sir!

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.430
Good. Everyone move out!

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.340
Sir!

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:01.070
Come on Rygart,

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:03.650
let's go.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:07.540
All right.

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:14.110
Loggin!

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.060
You're alive!

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.910
Narvi? What's happened?

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:23.730
Your uniform's in tatters.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.730
Nile!

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:31.230
You're not his ghost, are you?

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:37.040
Nope. Strange as it may seem, I'm still alive.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:44.740
So what do we do?

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:47.760
Athens' battalion is heading for Binonten.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.860
We've got to circle around somehow and rejoin our forces.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:55.130
Somehow? You're telling me to floor this
battered Golem through total darkness?

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:57.060
What if the enemy sees us?

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.790
Then we can score some ammo!

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:00.930
Really?

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:03.280
We just have to catch them off guard!

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:07.640
Well, I guess this thing isn't exactly in fighting condition...

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:14.640
The materials have arrived! Send a report to Queen Sigyn!

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.760
Request more ships for the evacuees!

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.610
Isn't that a little more important?

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:24.100
The quartz I've ordered is much sturdier than anything you might find in Krisna.

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:28.310
Please be careful or else you'll break the machines.

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:29.150
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:31.750
Also, be sure to complete it posthaste.

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:32.350
Understood!

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:42.240
What should I do, Gram?

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:57.080
We're able to house the remaining 20 percent of the city's
evacuees, but factoring in the northern villagers...

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.190
We've been able to secure several vessels.

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:01.420
What about our food and water reserves?

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:03.100
At most, we have two month's worth.

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:08.000
Very good. That will buy us some time to repel Orlando.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.040
Are you mad?!

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:13.930
General Borcuse is leading a whole battalion here!

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:17.160
He'll likely arrive tomorrow morning.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:21.760
We have a mere 60 golems to defend ourselves—
if he manages to breach our walls then—

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:23.250
Enough, Commander Konoe.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.590
I am well aware of our situation.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:38.600
<i>Can we triumph over against incredible odds?</i>

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:56.450
We stand little chance of beating Borcuse to the capital!

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.880
We'll likely have to engage them without resupplying.

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.400
Yes, sir!

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:07.340
Rygart! We may encounter the enemy
before the Delphine comes back online.

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:10.760
Rygart!

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:13.300
Gotcha. Just drop me off somewhere if we do.

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:18.330
I'll find a rock to crawl under.

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:21.410
Will do.

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:07.400
You're a godsend.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:11.130
I never thought we'd be able to
find such a large piece of quartz.

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:13.050
No trouble at all, milady.

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:17.530
Though I fear the grinders may not be able to handle the stress.

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:21.160
I'm not trying to tell you what to do.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:25.660
The end result is up to you, but I know of a cheaper, more efficient way to get started.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:29.060
Not to mention it'll save us some time.

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:30.750
Are you sure about this?

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:33.740
My ship is practically a mobile laboratory.

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:35.170
There's nothing I don't have!

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:42.190
They're here!

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:44.190
Approximately 90 in number!

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:46.740
Borcuse.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:50.260
I guess General Baldr wasn't fast enough.

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:51.140
Enemy forces spotted!

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:54.620
Establish the first line of defense!

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:01.420
Enemy forces!

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.310
Establish the first line of defense!

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:04.980
Formation one!

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:07.380
Do not let them set foot in our city!

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:07.990
Yes, ma'am!

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:10.000
Hurry, they're here!

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:18.600
Colonel Io,

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:21.500
the gates of the capital lie ahead.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.700
Let's knock and invite ourselves in.

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:25.040
Roger!

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:40.160
They're dispersing!

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:42.150
27 moving west, 18 advancing eastward!

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:45.170
So he insists on charging the front gate himself.

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:51.280
Open fire!

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:08.730
Have the townspeople all evacuated?

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:10.010
And the refugees?

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:12.650
Everyone that arrived up until now is safe.

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:16.680
Those who haven't have lost their chance.

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:21.630
We had men searching the area, but...

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:25.340
What do you think?

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:27.200
Astonishing...

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.660
Let's begin work on the next phase!

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:31.110
Are the ligaments ready?

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:05.530
<i>They've got us right where they want us.</i>

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:07.700
Cover me! I'll open the gate!

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:20.550
Leto?

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:25.470
I'll provide cover and sniping is my specialty, sir.

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:31.350
Excellent work!

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:48.440
Borcuse!

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:54.840
Well, aren't we brave?

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:05.220
Don't let them get inside!

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:13.240
Fall back to secondary positions!

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:14.760
Don't let them break through the northern gates!

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:27.550
There he is. Lady Siqwyn was right.

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:29.950
That's good enough.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:32.520
Let's attach the ligaments.

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:34.080
Is the reinforced quartz ready yet?

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:38.160
You want those giant ligaments to move?

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:41.120
They can’t move like normal ones do.

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:45.600
But we need something with the strength and flexibility to handle its large mass.

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:48.900
What about the joint ligaments?

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:52.590
Wait right there, I'll go get them!

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:54.330
Lady Sigyn, please wait!

00:15:57.940 --> 00:15:59.300
Your accuracy is commendable.

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:15.330
I cannot let you advance any further!

00:16:19.030 --> 00:16:24.170
I never expected to get this far with such a small force to begin with.

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:32.380
Looks like we’re losing the race to the guys at the east gate!

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:42.580
Secure all roads leading to the north gate!

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:43.450
Roger!

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:47.560
I'll take out their sniper!

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:50.320
Leto!

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:18.430
Each of you pick an opponent. Godspeed.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:19.440
Yes, sir!

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:32.630
Lady Sigyn.

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:34.460
Just a moment, please.

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:53.370
Sit down on the bed.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:54.000
What?

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:54.750
Hurry!

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:56.370
Yes!

00:17:59.420 --> 00:18:00.610
You can come in now.

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:04.380
Take this and this. Quickly.

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:05.940
You two at the door, please help assist us.

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.890
B-But...

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:09.500
Hurry. We don't have much time.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:10.830
Yes, ma'am!

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:11.870
These too, please.

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:14.300
Be extremely careful with them.

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:15.160
As you wish.

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:16.880
I'll be right behind you.

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:24.700
All clear.

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:31.690
I'm developing weaponry to fight off your nation's golems.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:33.400
...I know that.

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:36.550
But only the Delphine can use it.

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:39.480
I'll present it to Rygart when he returns.

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:43.430
I'm still awaiting news of his arrival, though.

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:49.350
But I know he'll come back. He swore he would.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:56.020
<i>I'll stop being angry once you come home safely.</i>

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:03.330
<i>Sure thing.</i>

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:12.710
Cleo, I want you to promise me something as well.

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:16.180
However...

00:19:17.660 --> 00:19:19.130
Sigyn!

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:29.620
Del...

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:34.600
It's time for us to go.

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:47.260
Where do you think you're going?

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:48.640
Stop him!

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:51.390
Fire!

00:20:51.820 --> 00:20:52.900
Not like this!

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.900
What went through your
mind when you saw the villagers?

00:21:12.510 --> 00:21:13.660
What will you do?

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:16.120
Krisna is as good as finished!

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.890
You filthy barbarians!

00:21:17.890 --> 00:21:20.700
“That's war. There's nothing I could do?”

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:23.380
Don't let the deaths of strangers weigh too heavily on you.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:25.040
It's not your problem.

00:22:05.030 --> 00:22:05.950
Del.

00:23:51.120 --> 00:23:52.570
This isn't the end is it?

00:23:53.340 --> 00:23:55.300
They'll come back, right?

00:23:55.770 --> 00:23:59.020
Endless fate, eternal recurrence.
